  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac12x^2$. Find the value(s) of $x$ for which $f(f(x))=x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0,2$.\n\nSubstitute into the outer function, then factorise the resulting equation.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac12\\left(\\frac12x^2\\right)^2\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac18x^4\\end{align*}$$\nThus the required equation is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac18x^4&=x\\\\x^4-8x&=0\\\\x(x^3-8)&=0\\\\x(x-2)(x^2+2x+4)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x^2+2x+4=(x+1)^2+3>0$ for real $x$, the solutions are $x=0$ and $x=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
